<title>YUGOSLAVIA: Yugoslav Sept trade gap $130 mln vs $98 mln in Aug.</title>
<headline>Yugoslav Sept trade gap $130 mln vs $98 mln in Aug.</headline>
<dateline>BELGRADE 1996-10-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Statistical Office reported the following economic indicator details.</p>
<p> YUGOSLAV TRADE	SEPT 96    AUG 96	SEPT 95</p>
<p> Exports million USD  154	  155	    n.a.</p>
<p> Imports		  284	  253	    n.a.</p>
<p> Balance		 -130	 - 98	    n.a.</p>
<p>CUMULATIVE FIGURES (JANUARY TO SEPT)</p>
<p> Exports million USD 1,259	1,101	    n.a.</p>
<p> Imports		 2,655	2,265	    n.a.</p>
<p> Balance		-1,396     -1,164	    n.a.</p>
<p>NOTES -- Data refers to rump Yugoslavia, comprising Serbia and Montenegro.</p>
<p>Comparative figures for the previous year are not available as the country was under an international trade embargo which was lifted on October 1 after nearly four and a half years. -- Amra Kevic, Belgrade newsroom +381 11 2224305</p>
</text>
